WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.170
Holy crap! Are you kiddin' me?

3
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:40.200
<b>Leader of the Mt. Atama Thieves,
Ashura Doji</b>

4
00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.250
The Oniwabanshu are down.

5
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:39.500
The Mimawari-gumi are toast.

6
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.220
We got no one left!

7
00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.580
reputation,
but I wasn't expecting this!

8
00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:54.500
He didn't just resist the virus,

9
00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.790
he used its power
to wreck our troops!

10
00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.000
I see why the Land of
Wano has remained

11
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.090
untouched for so many years.

12
00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:03.840
It's an island of monsters.

13
00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.560
What are you
waiting for, Yatappe?

14
00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:28.230
Empty your mind
and calm yourself!

15
00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.760
You know what'll happen
if I become an oni!

16
00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:40.650
I'm sorry, please give
me a second to compose myself!

17
00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:44.480
I-I'll do it soon.
I-I'll do it now!

18
00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.560
I do not envy you.

19
00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.400
Of course, it's hard.

20
00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.690
He is like a father to us!

21
00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.870
I'm losing control,
Tsunagoro, do it!

22
00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.290
You won't go alone, Boss.

23
00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.330
I shall be with you soon!

24
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.300
Omasa, no!

25
00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.760
C'mon, please!

26
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.920
Can't you help them,
Mister Raccoon?

27
00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.110
There's no time!

28
00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:20.070
There's no saving me anymore.

29
00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.610
You don't have to be afraid.

30
00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:28.080
Now cut me down!
I don't want to hurt you!

31
00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:36.140
If you don't do it, I won't
be able to control myself!

32
00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:40.350
We have done our best,
but this is it, Mister Raccoon.

33
00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.770
If we don't get that cure now,

34
00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.360
this whole floor,
all of our friends,

35
00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.230
will become Ice Oni again!

36
00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.980
Help us, Master Queen!

37
00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:56.570
Master Queen!

38
00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.780
All of your men have
served you faithfully.

39
00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:03.080
Why do we have to die from
your virus alongside the enemy?

40
00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:08.250
I know you

41
00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.920
Why should I
lift a finger for you?

42
00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.590
You peons aren't worth saving!

43
00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:16.220
You ever consider that?

44
00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.260
Listen, morons,
if I don't have any use for you,

45
00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.100
then you're no better
than garbage!

46
00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.240
Show some respect.

47
00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.950
That virus is my masterpiece!

48
00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:36.620
In fact, it was created
to erase your deficiencies.

49
00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.790
You hear that, Pleasures?

50
00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.870
You already lost the Devil Fruit
lottery, so it's not like you're

51
00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.960
gonna ever amount to anything!

52
00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.670
You're nothing but
giggling cannon fodder!

53
00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:49.170
How

54
00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.380
As for you Waiters.

55
00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.300
No matter how long you wait,
no more SMILE Fruits are coming.

56
00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.970
You lost your chance!

57
00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:00.560
You're no better
than the Pleasures!

58
00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:04.140
"The Eternal Waiters,"
a living tragedy!

59
00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.520
A colossal monument to failure!

60
00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:09.230
The only way you scrubs
can help the Beast Pirates

61
00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:12.240
is to become an oni
and cause some chaos

62
00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.990
before you kick the bucket!

63
00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:15.110
Ya dig?

64
00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:18.320
It's better to burn out
than fade away.

65
00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:22.290
Wait. This is like
you're telling us to die?

66
00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.580
And why not?

67
00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.630
We have more than enough troops.

68
00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:32.460
How could you say that?

69
00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:33.800
You're sick!

70
00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.010
I gave you a chance!

71
00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:40.220
That antibody could save
a couple of you at least!

72
00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:47.600
Damn it!
I'm not gonna die like this!

73
00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.100
Cut down the samurai!

74
00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.270
Cut down the oni!

75
00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:51.730
Every man for himself!

76
00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:56.240
Now you're motivated!

77
00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.320
Some of you might even survive!

78
00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:00.780
This guy is a monster.

79
00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.450
I can't believe they follow him!

80
00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:04.500
Well, that's pirates for you.

81
00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:07.540
Listen up, you damn samurai!

82
00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:11.590
You might wanna think about what
you're protecting right now!

83
00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:14.460
That raccoon made
some big promises,

84
00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:18.260
but he's a pirate just like us!

85
00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:19.800
Don't you dare!

86
00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:23.640
You really think he can mass
produce antibodies that quickly?

87
00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.180
He tricked you!

88
00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.190
He was infected as well!

89
00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.230
He probably took
the antibody for himself

90
00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:32.980
and got the hell out!

91
00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:37.490
The Straw Hats are
nothing like you!

92
00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:39.740
How can you be so sure?

93
00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:43.200
You think pirates have morals?

94
00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:48.420
This may be farewell for now,

95
00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:52.210
but I'll follow you
sooner or later, Boss!

96
00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.420
Don't be so hasty to follow.

97
00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:03.320
We love you, Boss!

98
00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.410
Farewell.

99
00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:31.150
What the hell?

100
00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:35.700
Please, Mister Raccoon,
don't try and stop me!

101
00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.200
We're losing him!
This was his choice!

102
00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.700
I'm going to save him!

103
00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:42.500
Stand back and watch!

104
00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:47.460
This will work!
Swallow it, Boss!

105
00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:53.680
That was close!
You guys scared me!

106
00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.140
So, did that fix him?

107
00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:02.640
All right! It's working fine!

108
00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.770
See? His body's warming up!

109
00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:23.070
You're not
dead, are you?

110
00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:24.660
Tell me you're alive, Boss!

111
00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:27.480
I am!

112
00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.900
Yes, I knew you could
do it, Mister Raccoon-Dog!

113
00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.740
The boss is okay!

114
00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:40.360
Miyagi! Tristan!
You better hurry!

115
00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:42.860
We're on it, Dr. Chopper!

116
00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:46.400
Is that a cannon?

117
00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:52.910
Okay, it's ready!
Just give the word!

118
00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:56.120
Oh! Lemme get on top!

119
00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:01.670
Dr. Chopper! Do the honors!

120
00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:03.590
Wait, what?

121
00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:10.510
It's my Chopperphage Nebulizer!

122
00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.740
<b>N
E
B
U
L
I
Z
E
R</b>
<b>C
H
O
P
P
E
R
P
H
A
G
E</b>

123
00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:13.850
Fire!

124
00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:39.140
What the hell
do you think you're doing,

125
00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:42.230
you damn raccoon?

126
00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:46.310
You've destroyed my masterpiece!

127
00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:49.980
How did you even pull that off?!

128
00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.610
Even with a cure,
it's impossible to

129
00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:55.320
give the medicine to
everyone on the floor,

130
00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.530
since you made sure to
infect so many people!

131
00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.160
So, I crafted a virus
out of the antibody!

132
00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.330
One that spreads just as fast!

133
00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:03.920
You what?

134
00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:07.710
If you can make a bad virus,
I can beat it with a good virus!

135
00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:10.590
I had to get creative and
distribute it through mist,

136
00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:14.300
but all they need to do
is breathe it in.

137
00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.890
You're just a doctor from
a ratty little pirate crew!

138
00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:21.350
How the hell did you learn
a trick like that?

139
00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.430
Because our crew has
traveled the world

140
00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.940
and trained with the best!

141
00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:27.690
Also, you got some nerve
healing my flunkies!

142
00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:29.690
Stay in your lane, damn it!

143
00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.860
Their lives are mine!

144
00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.530
I'm cleaning up
your mess after you

145
00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.740
let a deadly virus
get out of hand!

146
00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:40.700
That isn't a weapon
you should use so lightly!

147
00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:47.010
I am a genius, dammit!

148
00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:47.160
You think I need a raccoon
to teach me ethics?

149
00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:50.000
you big stupid dummy?

150
00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:02.980
Pleasures?

151
00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:05.860
You saved me!

152
00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.610
Get outta my way!

153
00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:12.780
If you wanna die so bad,
then do it somewhere else!

154
00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:15.580
Shut up, Queen!

155
00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:18.960
Our brothers were almost
killed by you, and for what?

156
00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:21.750
Mister Raccoon here
saved our lives!

157
00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.750
So, tell me,
what do we have to gain

158
00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.050
working for a maniac like you?

159
00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:30.010
At least we can die for
someone worth protecting!

160
00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:32.680
Ain't that right, guys?
Let's hear it!

161
00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.230
Thanks, Mister Raccoon!

162
00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:37.600
Raccoon!

163
00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:40.720
Tanuki!

164
00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:39.060
Mister Raccoon!

165
00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.680
Tanuki!

166
00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:42.860
No, Doctor Raccoon!

167
00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:45.730
We are in your debt,
Mr. Tanuki!

168
00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:45.900
I'm forever in your debt,
Mister Raccoon!

169
00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:48.360
Mister Raccoon,
that was amazing!

170
00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.190
Mr. Tanuki... Thank you!

171
00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:51.520
You're really somethin' else,
little tanuki.

172
00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:51.990
The Straw Hats are lucky.
That's one good raccoon!

173
00:11:51.990 --> 00:12:01.670
Go, Raccoon! You're the best!

174
00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:03.840
You can go to hell, Queen!

175
00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:11.050
You think I need you chumps?

176
00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:16.430
What the hell is this?

177
00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:18.890
Nice work back there, Raccoon!

178
00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:21.810
Now do it!

179
00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:23.520
You got it, Marco!

180
00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.320
But there's one last thing
I wanna say.

181
00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:29.900
I'll kill you, Raccoon!

182
00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:31.490
Rumble!

183
00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:34.070
Monster Point!

184
00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:50.080
We're so sorry!

185
00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:53.380
<b>Right-Brain Tower

Inside the Dome</b>

186
00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:54.960
If we climb through the ceiling,

187
00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.670
we can hide in the space
between the floors.

188
00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.800
I doubt anyone will
look for us in there!

189
00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:00.090
That's good!

190
00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.550
Lord Momonosuke,
hang on a little while longer!

191
00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:05.260
Be brave, Momonosuke!

192
00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.220
I know you can do this!

193
00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:09.180
In truth,
my heart is in turmoil.

194
00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:17.080
Yamato and I have dispatched
every foe in sight.

195
00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:20.790
Not because of our foes,
but because of my helplessness.

196
00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.830
I'm a useless burden.

197
00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.070
Enough, you all think
far too highly of me!

198
00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:32.660
I'm nothing. Nothing!

199
00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.240
I am but a fool!

200
00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.870
I am spineless and weak!

201
00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:41.170
I'm not worth defending.

202
00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.790
Just let me die.

203
00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:45.840
I think you're
perfectly great, my lord!

204
00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.970
There's nothing great about me!

205
00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:51.300
You must give yourself
time to grow!

206
00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:54.220
Yes, you may be small
right now, but someday,

207
00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.850
I know you'll grow into
a fine shogun!

208
00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.850
You'll be a great man someday!

209
00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:01.440
You can surpass
even Kozuki Oden!

210
00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:04.440
You're just saying that.

211
00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:07.900
It's not true.
It's not true at all!

212
00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:12.200
I am a failure!

213
00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.910
Huh? You're an eel?

214
00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.580
Lord Momonosuke!

215
00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.460
I'm afraid I don't understand.

216
00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:23.460
This happens when he's troubled.

217
00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.840
He's unable to return
to his human form

218
00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:27.960
until his heart is at ease.

219
00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:29.920
But you weren't born this way.

220
00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:32.260
Momo, did you eat a Devil Fruit?

221
00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.260
I did.

222
00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:39.730
<b>Guest Parlor

Inside the Castle</b>

223
00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:47.380
Speaking of Kaido.

224
00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:51.680
Remember when the Navy captured
him all those years ago?

225
00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:55.720
Doctor Vegapunk
took the opportunity

226
00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:58.350
to extract his
Bloodline Elements.

227
00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:01.730
Then made an artificial
Devil Fruit from it.

228
00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:05.360
Naturally, the World Government
asked him to hand it over,

229
00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:07.360
but in the end his
creation was viewed

230
00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:09.450
as a disappointing failure.

231
00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:11.820
However, they kept
the fruit on Punk Hazard

232
00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:13.950
instead of throwing it away.

233
00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:17.370
Why are you
bringing that up now?

234
00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.920
Punk Hazard was wiped out.

235
00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:22.080
It's nothing more than memory.

236
00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:25.300
I hope it was
destroyed in the explosion,

237
00:15:25.300 --> 00:15:28.340
but a team from Naval Base
G-5 reported that

238
00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:32.050
one facility on the island
was still in operation.

239
00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:35.750
Well, if it was a failure,

240
00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:39.170
at least we know there won't be
another Kaido out there.

241
00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:48.220
"Treasury"

242
00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:53.960
Who was it that patched us up?

243
00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:55.920
That's still a mystery.

244
00:15:55.920 --> 00:16:00.970
I thought I saw our benefactor.
But no, I must've been dreaming.

245
00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.070
I dare say it's impossible.

246
00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:09.660
While we sit here,
Sir Luffy and his friends

247
00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:12.240
are fighting Kaido
on our behalf.

248
00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:13.490
Even if we are injured,

249
00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:16.120
we must return
to the battle at hand.

250
00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.540
We cannot relent
until victory is ours.

251
00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:21.670
Let us go!

252
00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:24.550
While we still have
our lives to give!

253
00:16:25.990 --> 00:16:28.040
My loyal retainers!

254
00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:28.280
You've have had a rough
run of it, haven't you?

255
00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:30.720
You've had a rough
run of it, haven't you?

256
00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:33.750
How I've missed you all!

257
00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:42.090
I see the years haven't
been kind to you!

258
00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:55.100
It's... It's Lord Oden!

259
00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:03.680
I can't blame you
for being surprised.

260
00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:06.770
I was sent to the future
thanks to Toki's power.

261
00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:08.690
I shall explain it later.

262
00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:10.310
What a tale!

263
00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:14.480
My Lord Oden.
It's truly a miracle.

264
00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:18.640
Sorry to make you wait!

265
00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:20.980
But we'll have time
to celebrate our reunion

266
00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:23.270
once the battle is won!

267
00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:26.230
Now follow me!

268
00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:29.990
We failed to slay Kaido once,
but not this time!

269
00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:31.280
Of course!

270
00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:32.660
We shall come with you.

271
00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.790
I could ask for nothing more!

272
00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:35.960
Let us go forth.

273
00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:42.630
My samurai,
you're as loyal as you were

274
00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:43.840
the day we parted!

275
00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:50.110
This can't be Lord Oden.

276
00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:52.020
Who are you? Answer me!

277
00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:54.060
Ashura. My friend!

278
00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:55.400
Kin'emon!

279
00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:58.790
What did Lady Toki say?

280
00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:02.290
We may lack the power needed
to return to the past,

281
00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:04.880
however, we're able
to leap ahead.

282
00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:12.180
The past cannot be altered,
no matter what!

283
00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:15.680
Lady Toki was only able to
send people to the future,

284
00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:18.300
but she couldn't have
done that to Lord Oden.

285
00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:20.020
They both died.

286
00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:24.440
The history of that dark day
cannot be re-written.

287
00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:28.690
All we can do is bury our regret
and fight for tomorrow.

288
00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:34.630
Just so! And we'll do it
beside our lord!

289
00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:39.300
That's no
justification, Lord Oden!

290
00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.260
I've had enough!

291
00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:43.540
He's right!

292
00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:45.550
Huh?

293
00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:48.510
Come to your senses, Kin'emon!

294
00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:56.810
Look! He's not even bleeding!

295
00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:00.940
Oh, Ashura.

296
00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:02.740
What shameful behavior
from a man

297
00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:05.360
who pledged his
undying loyalty to me!

298
00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:10.900
What say you?
Will you be my samurai?

299
00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:14.200
Watch out!

300
00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:16.060
Kin'emon, I've heard
word of your courage!

301
00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:17.290
Ashura!

302
00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:20.120
Thank you for protecting
Momonosuke in my stead.

303
00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:29.020
You've shown
your true colors, haven't you?

304
00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:33.570
We all felt the same.

305
00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:36.780
I wish that Lord Oden
had returned to us.

306
00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:40.230
But this is a snake
in his guise!

307
00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:41.780
What a cruel trick!

308
00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:44.740
But if that's not Lord Oden,
then who are we dealing with?

309
00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:47.620
He'll pay for
getting my hopes up!

310
00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.870
Ashura! Are you all right?
Just hang in there!

311
00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:58.670
His voice. The way he acted.

312
00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:01.300
It was just like our lord.

313
00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:04.210
Only one man could mimic
Lord Oden so well.

314
00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:05.230
It's him.

315
00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:08.300
Reveal yourself!

316
00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:13.570
Kanjuro!

317
00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:15.740
How could you
say such a thing?

318
00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:18.460
Of course I'm Oden!

319
00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:20.790
You're hurt because
of my mistake!

320
00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:26.110
I failed to finish him.
Kanjuro should be dead.

321
00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:31.590
Even a sharp sword becomes dull
when pointed at a friend.

322
00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:36.930
Never apologize for
your kind heart.

323
00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:39.810
This is
nothing but a drawing!

324
00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:41.650
Then where's Kanjuro?

325
00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:46.400
I'm manipulating
the drawing from a distance!

326
00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:48.320
Unfortunately,
it's rather exhausting.

327
00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:50.360
especially since I'm injured.

328
00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:55.030
Hear that, Kiku?

329
00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:58.120
From my perspective,
your blade was plenty sharp.

330
00:20:58.120 --> 00:20:59.870
In fact, I am certain
that this battle

331
00:20:59.870 --> 00:21:02.750
will be my final performance.

332
00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:06.300
But I have an unrelenting
force that pushes me on.

333
00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:09.880
My revenge towards
the Kozuki Clan!

334
00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:12.010
So I can't die just yet.

335
00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:15.220
I shall pierce the heart
of the Kozuki Clan.

336
00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:17.850
And I'll make certain to
do it with my own blade!

337
00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:27.400
No. Lord Momonosuke's in danger!

338
00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:29.270
I heard a voice earlier.

339
00:21:29.270 --> 00:21:31.360
An announcement, I think.

340
00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:33.010
It said that Lord Momonosuke
was with a kunoichi.

341
00:21:33.010 --> 00:21:34.570
Momonosuke.

342
00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:36.860
Shinobu!

343
00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:39.370
In that case, we might
be able to reach her!

344
00:21:39.370 --> 00:21:39.490
All I want to do
is die in peace,

345
00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:41.280
All I want to do is die in peace

346
00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:43.450
and you'd take that
away from me?

347
00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:49.380
You've already lost!

348
00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:52.670
You'll die here,
unable to stop me!

349
00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:57.510
And your dear "Lord Oden"
will join you!

350
00:22:02.930 --> 00:22:06.060
Don't you think he'd want
to go out with a bang?

351
00:22:10.940 --> 00:22:12.980
Don't be angry!

352
00:22:14.570 --> 00:22:19.110
We'll die together!
Like good friends should!

353
00:22:26.520 --> 00:22:27.940
How's that?

354
00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:39.360
We lost our lord and
couldn't even avenge him!

355
00:22:39.360 --> 00:22:41.030
Of course you would
look for hope.

356
00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:42.870
It's our moment of defeat!

357
00:22:45.910 --> 00:22:48.250
Sir Luffy and his friends
are out there fighting

358
00:22:48.250 --> 00:22:51.670
with all their might to
liberate the Land of Wano!

359
00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:54.750
That is the reality we face.

360
00:23:02.470 --> 00:23:04.010
We can't.

361
00:23:25.410 --> 00:23:26.950
But how?

362
00:23:58.430 --> 00:24:02.770
And now, the climax, when I
shall play the lead at last.

363
00:24:04.860 --> 00:24:05.360
First, I embody the Kozuki,

364
00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:09.110
then I eliminate
the Kozuki, and die!

365
00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:13.400
An immaculate final act!

366
00:24:13.400 --> 00:24:15.570
What a beautiful play
my life has been,

367
00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:17.990
with all its twists and turns!

368
00:24:34.510 --> 00:24:36.340
You bastard.

369
00:24:36.340 --> 00:24:39.470
Fine then!
But we're in a hurry.

370
00:24:39.470 --> 00:24:41.680
What a pain in my ass.

371
00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:45.190
They sought to
protect their kings.

372
00:24:45.190 --> 00:24:49.150
Mere insects
standing in my path.

373
00:24:54.990 --> 00:24:56.320
Good luck.

374
00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:59.200
Protect Lord Momonosuke.

375
00:24:59.200 --> 00:25:01.370
Come on, Kin. Let's move.

376
00:25:01.370 --> 00:25:02.950
Very well.

377
00:25:02.950 --> 00:25:04.660
Please do not tarry.

378
00:25:04.660 --> 00:25:07.470
Good luck, we're all
counting on you.

379
00:25:07.470 --> 00:25:09.140
Denjiro, you traitor!

380
00:25:13.130 --> 00:25:13.150
So the "King of
the Day" thinks he can

381
00:25:13.150 --> 00:25:15.420
So the King of the Day
thinks he can defeat me

382
00:25:15.420 --> 00:25:16.280
defeat me all on his own?

383
00:25:16.280 --> 00:25:17.800
all on his own?

384
00:25:17.800 --> 00:25:21.600
We've both been injured.
Quite the matchup.

385
00:25:21.950 --> 00:25:23.790
Make no mistake.

386
00:25:23.790 --> 00:25:27.000
I didn't stay behind
to settle a score.

387
00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:29.210
I came to put an end to this.

388
00:25:29.210 --> 00:25:29.320
You-gara have created enough
victims, Jack! It's over!

389
00:25:29.320 --> 00:25:32.410
You-gara have created
enough victims, Jack!

390
00:25:32.410 --> 00:25:33.870
It's over!

391
00:25:34.370 --> 00:25:36.870
You have no moon to rely on.

392
00:25:36.870 --> 00:25:39.130
And you have no poison.

393
00:25:42.980 --> 00:25:46.740
Seems we both will
have to make do.

394
00:26:02.130 --> 00:26:05.260
We gotta put this
fire out, quick!

395
00:26:05.260 --> 00:26:08.600
The water's run out!
Bring me more!

396
00:26:09.930 --> 00:26:11.350
Huh?

397
00:26:21.110 --> 00:26:23.860
What the hell? No, it can't be.

398
00:26:23.860 --> 00:26:27.370
I'm going to relish
making you traitors pay!

399
00:26:27.370 --> 00:26:30.290
I was sure...
Your head came off!

400
00:26:41.850 --> 00:26:45.640
You thought you
could betray me, Kaido? Hmph.

401
00:26:48.730 --> 00:26:51.100
Even a beheading
can't keep you down.

402
00:26:51.100 --> 00:26:53.730
I'm sure you're not eager
for a second one.

403
00:26:53.730 --> 00:26:55.690
Quite rude of Kaido.

404
00:26:55.690 --> 00:26:57.870
Wouldn't you say?

405
00:26:57.870 --> 00:27:00.500
I'll burn this castle
to the ground!

406
00:27:00.500 --> 00:27:01.960
When I'm done with it,

407
00:27:01.960 --> 00:27:05.300
Onigashima will be nothing
but a ball of fire!

408
00:27:05.300 --> 00:27:07.590
There's no escape up here.

409
00:27:07.590 --> 00:27:09.760
And no way out!

410
00:27:13.100 --> 00:27:16.560
Every last one of you will die!

411
00:27:16.560 --> 00:27:19.890
That's the cost of betraying me!

412
00:27:30.340 --> 00:27:31.840
Momonosuke.

413
00:27:31.840 --> 00:27:34.130
Could you try to change
back to normal please?

414
00:27:34.130 --> 00:27:35.720
You kind of stick out.

415
00:27:35.720 --> 00:27:37.830
Oh. Right.

416
00:27:37.830 --> 00:27:39.000
Hm?

417
00:27:44.230 --> 00:27:47.270
Hang in there,
Lord Momonosuke, be brave.

418
00:27:47.270 --> 00:27:49.520
Sorry, I'm trying.

419
00:27:52.030 --> 00:27:53.280
Despite my shameful outburst,

420
00:27:53.280 --> 00:27:55.400
I have gotten better
at controlling it.

421
00:27:57.030 --> 00:27:59.370
When I first met
Luffy and his associates,

422
00:27:59.370 --> 00:28:01.540
I would transform into
a dragon every time

423
00:28:01.540 --> 00:28:03.580
I was surprised or became sad.

424
00:28:03.580 --> 00:28:07.440
I can't help but ask.
Is it like my father's power?

425
00:28:07.440 --> 00:28:10.110
I wish I could turn into
a monster like he does.

426
00:28:10.110 --> 00:28:10.170
At least I'd be of some
use to my friends.

427
00:28:10.170 --> 00:28:12.500
At least I'd be of
some use to my friends!

428
00:28:12.500 --> 00:28:14.170
Luffy is still
on the battlefield

429
00:28:14.170 --> 00:28:17.430
fighting my father as we speak,
so what are we waiting for?

430
00:28:17.470 --> 00:28:20.850
I should be fighting
Kaido as Oden!

431
00:28:20.850 --> 00:28:23.890
Luffy's power
seems to be waning,

432
00:28:23.890 --> 00:28:26.270
but for some reason,
he's in very high spirits!

433
00:28:26.270 --> 00:28:28.100
That's good. Huh?

434
00:28:31.360 --> 00:28:32.780
Wait, I don't understand.

435
00:28:32.780 --> 00:28:34.690
How can you tell?

436
00:28:37.470 --> 00:28:39.600
Huh? Anyone?

437
00:28:41.170 --> 00:28:43.460
How the hell are we
supposed to beat these two?

438
00:28:45.670 --> 00:28:49.300
Everything we do
bounces right off of them.

439
00:28:50.640 --> 00:28:52.180
I guess Emperors of the Sea

440
00:28:52.180 --> 00:28:54.140
are just built different.

441
00:28:54.140 --> 00:28:55.720
They trying to show off?

442
00:28:55.720 --> 00:28:58.100
They can at least pretend
we've got a chance.

443
00:28:59.230 --> 00:29:02.690
Just keep at it.

444
00:29:02.690 --> 00:29:05.780
Our attacks have to be
doing something to them!

445
00:29:05.780 --> 00:29:08.070
They're human, aren't they?

446
00:29:09.860 --> 00:29:12.410
Gum-Gum...

447
00:29:16.160 --> 00:29:18.540
You did that earlier
and it didn't work!

448
00:29:18.540 --> 00:29:20.330
Think before you attack!

449
00:29:20.330 --> 00:29:23.550
You say they're human,
but they're nothing like us.

450
00:29:23.550 --> 00:29:25.100
That much is clear.
They're demonic.

451
00:29:25.100 --> 00:29:26.180
So what?

452
00:29:26.180 --> 00:29:27.560
If you don't think
you can beat them,

453
00:29:27.560 --> 00:29:29.100
then why are you here?

454
00:29:29.100 --> 00:29:32.070
I'm just saying we need to
come up with a good plan first!

455
00:29:32.070 --> 00:29:35.030
We should pull
one of them away from here.

456
00:29:35.030 --> 00:29:36.470
Now you're talking.

457
00:29:36.470 --> 00:29:36.570
Those two side-by-side are
quite the gruesome spectacle.

458
00:29:36.570 --> 00:29:40.660
Those two side by side are
quite the gruesome spectacle.

459
00:29:43.430 --> 00:29:46.460
A literal vision of hell.

460
00:30:12.670 --> 00:30:14.510
You think this is the first time

461
00:30:14.510 --> 00:30:16.700
I've been through hell?

462
00:30:17.540 --> 00:30:19.380
You always have that
glimmer in your eye,

463
00:30:19.380 --> 00:30:21.390
even when the stakes are down!

464
00:30:24.100 --> 00:30:26.890
You ready to die, boy?

465
00:30:26.890 --> 00:30:29.510
You first, old man.
